WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.550
Paging and throttling are
where clients quietly break.

2
00:00:03.550 --> 00:00:07.188
When Graph returns a next link,
the client follows it to the end,

3
00:00:07.188 --> 00:00:11.467
and it sends the same headers on every
page, because Learn says they aren't

4
00:00:11.467 --> 00:00:15.675
carried forward by default, and an
advanced query changes without them.

5
00:00:15.675 --> 00:00:19.787
When Graph says slow down, the
client waits as long as it's told.

6
00:00:19.787 --> 00:00:23.976
When it isn't told, which really
happens for Conditional Access,

7
00:00:23.976 --> 00:00:25.426
it backs off, with a cap.

8
00:00:25.426 --> 00:00:30.800
It also marks its requests as low priority,
so background reads give way to people.

9
00:00:30.800 --> 00:00:34.800
And inside a batch, it retries
throttled items itself.
